ents/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133446105,imgsize-1296528.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A British couple bought a derelict 85-foot, seven-storey Victorian water tower at auction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133445009.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Kennington, a neglected Victorian water tower dating back to 1877 has been transformed into a stunning family residence. This Grade II-listed landmark, originally built for an asylum, underwent a lavish restoration by a British couple. They incorporated a contemporary glass cube and an additional utility tower, resulting in a remarkable home boasting four bedrooms and panoramic views of the city.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-british-couple-bought-a-derelict-85-foot-seven-storey-victorian-water-tower-at-auction-after-years-of-painstaking-work-the-former-asylum-water-supply-became-their-family-home/articleshow/133445009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-british-couple-bought-a-derelict-85-foot-seven-storey-victorian-water-tower-at-auction-after-years-of-painstaking-work-the-former-asylum-water-supply-became-their-family-home/articleshow/133445009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-24T00:32:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133445967,imgsize-338758.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Wash rice twice, not 7 times: Drought-hit England targets faith, cultural habits]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133445641.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/wo